ISSUE TITLE: ROWS_SCANNED scan metric double-counts rows passing the filter when the scan uses the joined heap (essential column family filtering)
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
When a scan enables {{Scan#setLoadColumnFamiliesOnDemand(true)}} and its filter marks some column families as non-essential ({{{}Filter#isFamilyEssential{}}}, introduced by HBASE-5416), {{RegionScannerImpl}} populates a row in two steps: the essential families through the store heap and — only if the row passes the filter — the remaining families through the joined heap.

Both steps go through {{{}RegionScannerImpl#populateResult{}}}, which increments the ROWS_SCANNED metric ({{{}ServerSideScanMetrics.COUNT_OF_ROWS_SCANNED_KEY_METRIC_NAME{}}}, introduced by HBASE-5980) each time the given heap finishes the current row:


{code:java}
